+## Spring Boot Admin shows the Customer Core as OFFLINE
+
+The Customer Core requires mutual TLS on all of its endpoints, actuator
+endpoints included, so the monitoring server has to present a client
+certificate when it polls them. If `certs/spring-boot-admin.p12` and
+`certs/truststore.p12` are missing, the monitoring server logs
+
+```
+WARN c.l.s.MonitoringTlsConfiguration : No key or trust store found at ...
+```
+
+on startup and cannot reach the Customer Core, while the services it reaches
+over plaintext HTTP stay `UP`. Run `bash ./generate-certificates.sh` in the
+repository root and restart the monitoring server.
+
+A `No subject alternative DNS name matching ... found` error instead means the
+Customer Core registered under an address its certificate does not carry. The
+registered address is pinned with `spring.boot.admin.client.instance.service-base-url`
+in `customer-core/src/main/resources/application.properties`, and overridden to
+the Compose service name in `docker-compose.yml`.
+
